@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+---
+tier: spec
+created: 2026-09-20
+status: active
+owner: node
+branch: HEAD
+touches: [src/flask/ctx.py, src/flask/sansio/app.py, tests/test_appctx.py, tests/test_basic.py]
+---
+
+# teardown-cleanup
+
+## Why
+An exception in one teardown handler currently prevents later handlers and the
+corresponding teardown signal from running. Cleanup must be exhaustive without
+leaking an active context.
+
+## What
+- Run every registered request- and application-context teardown callback and
+  send each corresponding teardown signal even if earlier cleanup raises.
+- Raise collected cleanup failures only after the relevant cleanup completes;
+  use an exception group when the interpreter provides one.
+- Restore context-local state before a teardown failure leaves context popping.
+- Non-goal: change non-teardown signal dispatch semantics or callback order.
+
+## How
+- Use a common teardown runner to collect callback and signal-send failures.
+- Retain failures from request and application teardown while `AppContext.pop`
+  performs its remaining cleanup and resets its context variable.
+
+## Alternatives
+- Follows the existing reverse-registration callback order. A separate runner
+  per teardown path would duplicate error handling and could drift.
+
+## Impact
+- `AppContext.pop` is the common request, application-context, test-client,
+  and CLI cleanup path. Request teardown can include blueprint and app
+  handlers; application teardown is app-wide.
+- The public decorators and teardown signals retain their ordering and inputs;
+  only failure completion behavior changes. No data, permission, or migration
+  boundary is involved.
+
+## Acceptance
+- [x] Every request teardown callback and its teardown signal run after an earlier callback fails, and their failures remain observable — check: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_appctx.py -q`
+- [x] Every application-context teardown callback and its teardown signal run after an earlier callback fails, and their failures remain observable — check: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_appctx.py -q`
+- [x] A teardown error leaves no active application context — check: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_appctx.py -q`
+
+## Open questions
+None.
+
+## Decisions
+- context-teardown: callback and signal-send failures are collected in normal
+  execution order. Python 3.11+ raises their `BaseExceptionGroup`; Python 3.10
+  raises the first collected failure.
