+# context-teardown — delta
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+### Requirement: Exhaustive context teardown
+Flask SHALL attempt every registered request or application-context teardown
+callback and send its corresponding teardown signal, even if earlier teardown
+work raises an exception. It SHALL report collected teardown failures after
+cleanup finishes, as an exception group when supported by the interpreter and
+otherwise as the first collected failure. Context-local state SHALL be restored
+before that failure is reported.
+
+#### Scenario: Request teardown failure
+- WHEN a request teardown callback raises before later callbacks and the
+  request teardown signal
+- THEN later callbacks and the signal are attempted, all available teardown
+  failures are retained, and the request context is no longer active.
+
+#### Scenario: Application-context teardown failure
+- WHEN an application-context teardown callback raises before later callbacks
+  and the application-context teardown signal
+- THEN later callbacks and the signal are attempted, all available teardown
+  failures are retained, and the application context is no longer active.
+
